-- Tests for il-interpretation-definitions-ordinance.l4 (the entries of s 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance).
-- Expected values were decided from the words of each entry before the module was run; a failing assertion is a finding and
-- none was edited to match the code. Every fact is one the entry names. The comment above each group names the units of
-- the coverage table (NOTES.md section 2) that the group tests.

§ `Tests: the defined terms of Ordinance s 1`

§§ `Fixtures: statutes and instruments`

`a Knesset act` MEANS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS TRUE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS FALSE, `this Ordinance itself` IS FALSE)
`an ordinance of the Provisional Council` MEANS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS TRUE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS FALSE, `this Ordinance itself` IS FALSE)
`an ordinance of the Mandate` MEANS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS TRUE, `this Ordinance itself` IS FALSE)
`this Ordinance` MEANS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS FALSE, `this Ordinance itself` IS TRUE)
`not a statute` MEANS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS FALSE, `this Ordinance itself` IS FALSE)

`a Knesset act as an instrument` MEANS (`An instrument under the Ordinance` WITH `taken as a statute` IS (`A candidate statute under the Ordinance` WITH `a legislative act of the Knesset` IS TRUE, `an ordinance given by the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance lawfully given in Palestine before the State was established` IS FALSE, `this Ordinance itself` IS FALSE), `the statute it was given by virtue of` IS NOTHING, `given by virtue of an Act of the British Parliament or an Order in Council` IS FALSE, `a regulation, rule, by-law, proclamation, manifesto, order, direction, notice, announcement or other document` IS FALSE, `given by an authority in Palestine or in Israel` IS FALSE, `given on the basis of a regulation, rule or by-law of that kind` IS FALSE, `a regulation` IS FALSE, `a rule` IS FALSE, `a by-law` IS FALSE, `a manifesto` IS FALSE, `a proclamation` IS FALSE, `an order` IS FALSE, `a direction` IS FALSE, `a notice` IS FALSE, `an announcement` IS FALSE, `another document` IS FALSE)
