-- On the day the Law commenced a day-level date cannot say whether the enactment came before 00:01; the five repealed entries
-- answer FALSE either way, and every other entry REFUSES with the message of pass 1's `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced ...`.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance's definitions govern` `the Ordinance entry on "person"` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1) BECAUSE "a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day"
